{"requirements":[{"id":"monitoring_and_metrics","requirement":"node1 runs Prometheus monitoring node2, node3, and node4 through node_exporter on port 9100, using node-name targets, with current host metrics queryable on node1.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Final post-restart checks show the configured targets node2:9100, node3:9100, and node4:9100 all healthy. Prometheus returns fresh node_time_seconds values and node_uname_info mapping each target to its correct node name; node1 can also fetch each exporter directly.","evidence_ids":["cmd-469995fc3a7f425e","cmd-7254ed696af04608","global:after_executor:node2:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node3:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node4:listening-sockets"]},{"id":"prometheus_local_only","requirement":"The Prometheus interface on port 9090 is local to node1.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Prometheus listens only on 127.0.0.1:9090 and succeeds over loopback. Connections through node1's managed address and from node2 fail.","evidence_ids":["cmd-7254ed696af04608","cmd-77b5f0df58c24e79","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},{"id":"exporter_access_restricted","requirement":"Each node_exporter endpoint is limited to collection by node1.","status":"satisfied","summary":"After restart, every exporter listens only on its managed IPv4 address and retains ordered UFW rules allowing node1 followed by denial from anywhere else. Node1 successfully fetches all three endpoints, while non-node1 peers time out against each exporter.","evidence_ids":["cmd-cea2802e5c72488c","cmd-576b08c088a74d6e","cmd-d8bade2347924f6f","cmd-7254ed696af04608","cmd-77b5f0df58c24e79","cmd-a68226b2e51a4121"]}],"confidence":1,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified as retained or reverted. Package installation, hostname/configuration writes, firewall activation, and service changes directly supported the task. Reboots implemented the mandatory restart protocol. Disabling and resetting the package-induced failed OpenIPMI units remained in place but was justified cleanup, not unrelated experimentation. Final lifecycle observations show healthy package state, no failed services, and only the intended new listeners.","evidence_ids":["cmd-706aef7487bb44df","cmd-88b6667fc9844fd8","cmd-e3fac790444c451a","cmd-f14d276c464a41ab","cmd-4522c89906b0476f","cmd-19df769b0e6b461a","cmd-eff0e13d030c463b","cmd-414621fc39af429c","cmd-d08affcd9b3b4250","cmd-5545b49ad4884535","cmd-73e9bc138ed649e3","cmd-f851bf23ccfd4b85","cmd-1de453025a3e41a0","cmd-512e34ab238449a6","cmd-b27aaa4c5b1a444b","cmd-ff1b9b7ab955402a","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node3:failed-services","global:after_executor:node4:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health","global:after_executor:node3:package-health","global:after_executor:node4:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. The provider-wide restart protocol is complete for all four nodes: each has a healthy pre-restart state, acknowledged scheduled restart, changed boot identity, and recovered service, current metrics, and monitoring state. The post-restart identities also agree with all four fixed after-executor boot observations.","limitations":[]}
